    "reading": "11 of 21 committed models integrate position exactly (<1e-4 px residual against the velocity they advanced by), and 1 of those is still called kinematically inconsistent by the published predicate at a rate above 0.05. Recorded telemetry itself trips the predicate on 0.046 of frames because its velocity jumps on 0.030 of them, so the figure is partly a smoothness measurement and cannot be read as a consistency test alone. The ceiling classification is load-bearing in the chosen threshold: it accepts {'1.0': 3, '1.5': 3, '2.5': 9, '3.5': 9} records at ['1.0', '1.5', '2.5', '3.5'] px/frame respectively, and the 10.46 acceptances only appear at 2.5 px/frame or looser."
